00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:01.170
Why did we build this chip?

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:02.880
Because we wanted
to take machine

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:04.230
learning to the next level.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:06.600
We wanted to completely
optimize the experience

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:10.020
of running machine learning
computations in a data center.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:14.040
And this chip is 15
to 30 times faster

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.170
than a conventional
processor for machine

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:18.120
learning applications.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:20.880
Think about being seven
years in the future in terms

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:22.950
of what you're able to
do with your computer.

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:25.080
That's what we can
do with this chip.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:28.260
Now, how do we use this
internally at Google?

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:29.700
We use machine
learning at Google

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:34.500
to actually invest in how we
cool our own data centers.

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:37.500
Data center cooling is a really,
really complicated thing.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:40.320
You need to take into
account the weather outside,

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.845
the heat of the data center.

00:03:41.845 --> 00:03:43.470
You need to take into
account the pumps

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:45.015
and the pipes and the ducts.

00:03:45.015 --> 00:03:48.189
And it's a really complicated
equation for a human to solve.

00:03:48.189 --> 00:03:49.980
So we set up a machine
learning classifier.

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:52.800
And we asked to optimize all
the variables in the equation.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:55.200
And we were able to cut the
costs of cooling our data

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:58.092
